# Feature Modules

## App Page Wiring

Pages under `src/app/[locale]/({role})/` MUST only import the feature default export:

```tsx
import OperatorDashboard from "@/features/operator/dashboard/dashboard";

export default function OperatorDashboardPage() {
  return <OperatorDashboard />;
}
```

## Auth Features (strict split)

Every auth flow `{flow}` (e.g. `login`) uses this structure:

```
src/features/auth/{flow}/
  component/{flow}.component.tsx   # logic, UiForm, default export
  component/{flow}.view.tsx        # presentational UI + useTranslations
  schema/{flow}.schema.ts          # create{Flow}Schema(messages)
  type/{flow}.type.ts              # {flow}DefaultValues
  messages/en.json
  messages/ja.json
```

- NO barrel `index.ts` under auth features.
- App pages import `@/features/auth/{flow}/component/{flow}.component` only.
- View is imported ONLY by its sibling component (relative `./{flow}.view`).

## Non-Auth Features (operator, learner, etc.)

```
src/features/{role}/{name}/
  {name}.tsx              # default export, "use client" when interactive
  messages/en.json
  messages/ja.json
```

- Single feature file is acceptable for dashboards and CRUD screens.
- Colocate `messages/` in the same folder.
- Use `useTranslations` (client) or `getTranslations` (server) with the feature namespace.

## Message Namespace Conventions

| Area | JSON root key | Hook namespace |
|------|---------------|----------------|
| Auth | `Auth.{flow}` | `Auth.{flow}` |
| Operator | `operator{Name}` camelCase | `operatorDashboard`, `operatorTenant`, … |
| Learner | `Learner.{page}` | `Learner.dashboard`, … |
| Layouts | `layouts.{layout}` | `layouts.operatorLayout.sidebar` |

## New Feature Checklist

1. Create feature file(s) under `src/features/{role}/{name}/`.
2. Add `messages/en.json` + `messages/ja.json`.
3. Register in `src/i18n/message-registry.ts` AND `src/i18n/messages.ts`.
4. Create thin app page under the correct route group.
5. Never hardcode UI strings — see the translate rule.
